WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.112 --> 00:00:09.339
- Is it?
- Is it?

00:00:09.339 --> 00:00:10.334
- Is it?
- It is, right?

00:00:10.334 --> 00:00:11.900
- I don't know.
- I think it is.

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:16.803
("Good Old Boys")

00:00:16.803 --> 00:00:18.310
- I'm really excited to try out

00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:21.114
all these exotic American unknown things

00:00:21.114 --> 00:00:25.111
like chips and more chips.

00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:26.893
- This doesn't have a Mexican.

00:00:27.493 --> 00:00:28.582
What the hell?

00:00:28.936 --> 00:00:30.378
This has a Mexican.

00:00:30.378 --> 00:00:31.854
- I really don't get the point of

00:00:32.593 --> 00:00:35.496
making Mexican flavors
and calling it American.

00:00:36.189 --> 00:00:38.586
Again, it says hot sauce
and it's not spicy.

00:00:38.586 --> 00:00:40.943
- This is really, really spicy, man.

00:00:40.943 --> 00:00:42.893
- I think you guys
really underestimate us.

00:00:42.893 --> 00:00:45.027
We can have a lot of spice.

00:00:45.027 --> 00:00:47.170
- I'm saying that as an
Indian, this is spicy.

00:00:47.170 --> 00:00:48.623
- Ranch, I don't know what
ranch has to do with it.

00:00:48.623 --> 00:00:50.756
- I know flavors like apple or banana,

00:00:50.756 --> 00:00:53.479
but I don't know what
a cool ranch there was.

00:00:54.371 --> 00:00:55.185
- Not bad.

00:00:55.185 --> 00:00:56.689
- Oh.
- Not bad.

00:00:56.689 --> 00:00:57.400
- No.

00:00:57.400 --> 00:00:58.537
- So yeah, it's quite cheesy

00:00:58.537 --> 00:01:00.366
and it's lacking some flavor.

00:01:00.366 --> 00:01:01.280
- Not bad.

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:02.398
- My life's over.

00:01:02.398 --> 00:01:03.515
- This is the better one.

00:01:03.515 --> 00:01:04.832
This is the winner.

00:01:06.095 --> 00:01:07.396
- Onion rings and fun.

00:01:07.396 --> 00:01:08.594
- OK, they better be fun.

00:01:08.594 --> 00:01:09.570
They don't look fun.

00:01:09.570 --> 00:01:10.423
- There are no onions.

00:01:10.423 --> 00:01:11.337
- Hmm, they're Funyuns.

00:01:11.337 --> 00:01:12.292
- Smell of onion?

00:01:12.292 --> 00:01:12.902
- No.

00:01:12.902 --> 00:01:14.507
- Are these Funyuns or Pringles?

00:01:17.045 --> 00:01:18.064
- Oh yeah, that is good.

00:01:18.064 --> 00:01:20.006
- How do you actually have fun with this?

00:01:20.360 --> 00:01:22.107
- Bro, like this.

00:01:22.107 --> 00:01:22.960
- Bro, it's like--

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:24.240
- Bro, let's go like thug.

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:26.272
- Yeah, I could snack on this for hours.

00:01:26.272 --> 00:01:27.958
- I want some more rings.

00:01:27.958 --> 00:01:29.523
- No, no, no. I think this is...

00:01:29.523 --> 00:01:31.209
- Probably if I eat too much of this

00:01:31.209 --> 00:01:31.981
I'm gonna die.

00:01:31.981 --> 00:01:32.977
- On your knees, bro.

00:01:32.977 --> 00:01:33.964
Peace.

00:01:33.964 --> 00:01:36.016
- We don't really have turkey in India,

00:01:36.016 --> 00:01:37.784
not even the dried version.

00:01:37.784 --> 00:01:40.201
I've only had cooked meat.

00:01:40.970 --> 00:01:43.046
- I don't know if I wanna
put this in my mouth.

00:01:43.046 --> 00:01:45.545
- It doesn't look extremely
appetizing at all.

00:01:45.545 --> 00:01:47.698
- It's like a chicken that I bought

00:01:47.698 --> 00:01:48.998
and I kept it in the fridge,

00:01:48.998 --> 00:01:50.197
and I forgot about it.

00:01:50.197 --> 00:01:51.457
- I'm gonna break a tooth.

00:01:51.457 --> 00:01:53.675
- Let me just concentrate
on the chewing for a bit.

00:01:54.322 --> 00:01:55.073
- I give up.

00:01:55.073 --> 00:01:56.536
- It tastes normal, but--

00:01:56.536 --> 00:01:58.040
- It tastes good, but it's like--

00:01:58.040 --> 00:01:58.934
- It's tough, man.

00:01:58.934 --> 00:02:00.437
It's like chewing through rocks

00:02:00.437 --> 00:02:02.855
and then realizing that
there is nothing soft inside.

00:02:05.116 --> 00:02:07.168
- Yeah, it's just basically raw meat.

00:02:08.660 --> 00:02:09.642
I like it.

00:02:10.209 --> 00:02:10.941
- We get Cheetos here,

00:02:10.941 --> 00:02:13.521
but I've never heard of
flaming hot Cheetos--

00:02:13.521 --> 00:02:14.415
- Yeah.
- In my life.

00:02:14.415 --> 00:02:17.422
- It's exceptionally and alarmingly red.

00:02:17.422 --> 00:02:19.352
- Like a baby dragon.

00:02:19.352 --> 00:02:20.367
(Man in Red Shirt laughs)

00:02:20.367 --> 00:02:21.607
- This looks like kurkure.

00:02:21.607 --> 00:02:23.815
- Somebody put a lot of
Schezuan sauce on kurkure.

00:02:23.815 --> 00:02:24.909
- Plastic again.

00:02:25.725 --> 00:02:26.762
More plastic.

00:02:26.762 --> 00:02:27.411
- With cheese.

00:02:27.411 --> 00:02:28.264
- With cheese.

00:02:28.264 --> 00:02:29.768
- I love this.

00:02:29.768 --> 00:02:30.702
This is insane.

00:02:30.702 --> 00:02:32.125
- It's not flaming hot though.

00:02:32.125 --> 00:02:33.425
- The fire wants to come out.

00:02:33.425 --> 00:02:34.075
- Yeah.

00:02:34.075 --> 00:02:35.619
- But it just can't.

00:02:35.619 --> 00:02:37.183
- But it does taste really good.

00:02:37.183 --> 00:02:37.913
- This would do so good over here.

00:02:37.913 --> 00:02:38.908
- This will kill over here.

00:02:38.908 --> 00:02:40.879
- This would (bleep) kill over here.

00:02:40.879 --> 00:02:42.545
- Only thing about the American snacks,

00:02:42.545 --> 00:02:43.317
they lead astray.

00:02:43.317 --> 00:02:45.633
- Nah, nah. Indian snacks all the way.

00:02:45.633 --> 00:02:47.523
I like my samosas and my jelly bees.

00:02:47.523 --> 00:02:49.270
- Possibly can't imagine
myself having this

00:02:49.270 --> 00:02:51.058
again and again and again (mumbling).

00:02:51.058 --> 00:02:53.417
- You know the packaging
that these guys have is so

00:02:54.248 --> 00:02:55.321
in your face--
- It's very in your face.

00:02:55.321 --> 00:02:56.279
- Our product really good.

00:02:56.279 --> 00:02:58.392
- I hope you guys have rice and stuff

00:02:58.392 --> 00:02:59.835
somewhere in your diet

00:02:59.835 --> 00:03:04.000
because if you're having
Doritos every day, boy.

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:09.000
("Good Old Boys")

